      ],
      "orig": "15-DAY CONTINUATION OF NOTICE IS HEREBY GIVEN that the Department proposes amendments to sections 650, 672, 672.1, and 672.2 to Title 14, California Code of Regulations (CCR), for Invasive Mussels.",
      "text": "15-DAY CONTINUATION OF NOTICE IS HEREBY GIVEN that the Department proposes amendments to sections 650, 672, 672.1, and 672.2 to Title 14, California Code of Regulations (CCR), for Invasive Mussels."
    },
    {
      "self_ref": "#/texts/18",
      "parent": {
        "$ref": "#/body"
      },
      "children": [],
      "content_layer": "body",
      "label": "text",
      "prov": [
        {
          "page_no": 1,
          "bbox": {
            "l": 36.05,
            "t": 484.95,
            "r": 556.3580000000001,
            "b": 429.7220906282183,
            "coord_origin": "BOTTOMLEFT"
          },
          "charspan": [
            0,
            332
          ]
        }
      ],
      "orig": "The full text of the resulting amendment with the change clearly indicated, shall be made available to the public for at least 15 days before the agency amends, or repeals the resulting regulation. Any written comments received regarding the change will be responded to in the final statement of reasons required by Section 11346.9.",
      "text": "The full text of the resulting amendment with the change clearly indicated, shall be made available to the public for at least 15 days before the agency amends, or repeals the resulting regulation. Any written comments received regarding the change will be responded to in the final statement of reasons required by Section 11346.9."
    },
    {
      "self_ref": "#/texts/19",
      "parent": {
        "$ref": "#/body"
      },
      "children": [],
      "content_layer": "body",
      "label": "text",
      "prov": [
        {
          "page_no": 1,
          "bbox": {
            "l": 36.05,
            "t": 411.38,
            "r": 569.1999999999998,
            "b": 252.57209062821835,
            "coord_origin": "BOTTOMLEFT"
          },
          "charspan": [
            0,
            917
          ]
        }
      ],
      "orig": "On July 3, 2026, a notice of proposed action (NOPA) to adopt the above referenced regulations was distributed and noticed in compliance with Government Code section 11346.4. The NOPA stated that the Department was proposing to amend sections 650, 672, 672.1, and 672.2 to Title 14 of the CCR to expand the scope of the existing regulations to encompass all invasive mussel species, thereby ensuring consistency with the revised Fish and Game Code 2301, 2302, and new Fish and Game Code 2303 established by Assembly Bill 149. The proposed amendments incorporate components of prevention and containment to limit the spread of invasive mussels in California and to other states. Additionally, the proposal amends the Invasive Mussel Permit Application Form (DFW 1014), the Quarantine Notice Form (DFW 1015), the Administrative Penalty Form (DFW 1016), and creates a new Department Business List Request Form (DFW 1013).",
      "text": "On July 3, 2026, a notice of proposed action (NOPA) to adopt the above referenced regulations was distributed and noticed in compliance with Government Code section 11346.4. The NOPA stated that the Department was proposing to amend sections 650, 672, 672.1, and 672.2 to Title 14 of the CCR to expand the scope of the existing regulations to encompass all invasive mussel species, thereby ensuring consistency with the revised Fish and Game Code 2301, 2302, and new Fish and Game Code 2303 established by Assembly Bill 149. The proposed amendments incorporate components of prevention and containment to limit the spread of invasive mussels in California and to other states. Additionally, the proposal amends the Invasive Mussel Permit Application Form (DFW 1014), the Quarantine Notice Form (DFW 1015), the Administrative Penalty Form (DFW 1016), and creates a new Department Business List Request Form (DFW 1013)."
    },
    {
